# Go build artifacts
*.test
*.out
/bin/
/dist/

# scripts/release.sh's `mkdir -p dist release` output — the per-platform tarballs.
# Same class as /dist/ (tether#86). Nothing was ever committed here; this entry is
# what keeps it that way, since the published artifacts come from
# .github/workflows/release.yml and not from whatever a local run left behind.
/release/

# A compiled copy of ./cmd/build-hook, committed once on 2026-05-09 (3,001,974
# bytes) and referenced by nothing since (tether#86). Both callers —
# scripts/release.sh and .github/workflows/release.yml — build the wrapper to a
# temp path of their own, because it has to run on the host while the hook it
# produces is cross-compiled. The source stays; only the binary is ignored, so
# that `go build -o build-hook ./cmd/build-hook` cannot silently dirty the tree.
/build-hook

# Generated frontend bundle — `vite build` output, embedded into the binary by
# web/embed.go's `//go:embed all:dist`. Deliberately NOT committed (tether#81):
# a committed copy has no way to stay in sync with web/src, and any build that
# skips `pnpm build` (bare `go build`, `go install`) embeds that copy. It did go
# stale — one commit changed web/src without rebuilding it — with every test and
# CI job still green; the deploy that would have shipped the stale bundle was
# caught by hand, not by a gate.
#
# Consequence worth knowing before you clone: until web/dist exists, every go
# command that has to load the package graph — `go build`, `go vet`, `go test`,
# `go list ./...` — fails with
#   web/embed.go: pattern all:dist: no matching files found
# and `go list ./...` failing means gopls/your IDE will not load the module
# either. (`gofmt`, `go list -e ./...` and `go tool tygo generate` still work.)
# Run `make build` once. That loud failure is the point — it is what replaced the
# silent stale-SPA build.
#
# Keep scripts/check-artifacts-uncommitted.sh in sync with this block; CI runs
# it, so deleting these two entries turns CI red rather than quietly re-arming
# the bug.
/web/dist/

# `tsc -b` incremental caches — rewritten by every `pnpm build`. Same class as
# web/dist: build output that used to be tracked, which meant the mandatory
# build path always left the tree dirty and invited `git add -A` to re-commit it.
/web/*.tsbuildinfo

# Machine-readable test reports — rewritten by every `pnpm test` (tether#105).
# See the reporters block in web/vite.config.ts for why the run writes them at
# all. Same class again: generated, per-run, and therefore never committed —
# a tracked copy would be one more thing that is stale on every checkout, and
# the point of these files is that they describe *this* run.
/web/test-results/

# pnpm's install tree. It was committed by accident, not by decision (tether#86):
# two commits on 2026-05-09 added it, and in the first — titled "React 19+Vite 7
# SPA skeleton" — 2796 of the 2833 files were node_modules. None of the three
# reasons to vendor an install tree holds here, each checked rather than assumed:
# there is no offline build path anywhere in the repo (every `offline` hit is docs
# about PWA offline support, deferred to v0.5+); there is no patched dependency
# (no pnpm patch/resolutions/overrides keys, no patches/); and CI never read the
# committed copy — both workflows run `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` from the
# network, so the tracked tree was work for CI to reconcile, not work it saved.
#
# What it cost while tracked, measured at dbdfb24 on 2026-08-20: one
# `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` leaves 7264 dirty entries (7113 untracked, 137
# deleted, 14 modified) and nothing outside node_modules. So `git describe
# --tags --always --dirty` read `v0.5.0-110-gdbdfb24-dirty` after any build, which
# is the string scripts/build.sh compiles into the binary as its version.
#
# Keep scripts/check-artifacts-uncommitted.sh in sync with this block; CI runs it,
# so deleting this entry turns CI red rather than quietly re-arming the bug.
/web/node_modules/

# Spike output (per .plans Step 7) — runtime files only.
# Curated artifacts (the dated spike-report and verification-report from
# .plans Step 7 + Step 9) ARE checked in as evidence; everything else in
# spike-out/ is regenerated and gitignored.
/cmd/*/spike-out/*
!/cmd/spike/spike-out/2026-04-30-spike-report.md
!/cmd/spike/spike-out/2026-04-30-verification-report.md

# Editor/IDE
.vscode/
.idea/

# Local env
.env
.env.local

# OS
.DS_Store

# Local dev runtime state from scripts/dev.sh
.dev/

# A filled-in copy of deploy/tether.env.example holds the access token.
# deploy/tether.env is the obvious name to reach for; make it un-committable.
/deploy/tether.env
/deploy/*.env
